Metrics List:
- {"name": "container_ulimits_soft", "type": "gauge", "description": "Soft ulimit values for the container root process."}
- {"name": "container_fs_usage_bytes", "type": "gauge", "description": "Number of bytes that are consumed by the container on this filesystem."}
- {"name": "container_spec_memory_limit_bytes", "type": "gauge", "description": "Memory limit for the container."}
- {"name": "container_fs_limit_bytes", "type": "gauge", "description": "Number of bytes that can be consumed by the container on this filesystem."}
- {"name": "container_memory_usage_bytes", "type": "gauge", "description": "Current memory usage in bytes, including all memory regardless of when it was accessed"}
Question: Show the filesystem usage and limit bytes for all containers of the auth service.

Metrics List:
- {"name": "kube_replicaset_status_ready_replicas", "type": "gauge", "description": "[STABLE] The number of ready replicas per ReplicaSet."}
- {"name": "kube_deployment_status_replicas_ready", "type": "gauge", "description": "[STABLE] The number of ready replicas per deployment."}
- {"name": "kube_replicaset_status_replicas", "type": "gauge", "description": "[STABLE] The number of replicas per ReplicaSet."}
- {"name": "kube_deployment_status_replicas", "type": "gauge", "description": "[STABLE] The number of replicas per deployment."}
- {"name": "kube_replicaset_spec_replicas", "type": "gauge", "description": "[STABLE] Number of desired pods for a ReplicaSet."}
- {"name": "kube_deployment_spec_replicas", "type": "gauge", "description": "[STABLE] Number of desired pods for a deployment."}
- {"name": "kube_deployment_status_replicas_updated", "type": "gauge", "description": "[STABLE] The number of updated replicas per deployment."}
- {"name": "kube_deployment_status_replicas_unavailable", "type": "gauge", "description": "[STABLE] The number of unavailable replicas per deployment."}
- {"name": "kube_deployment_status_replicas_available", "type": "gauge", "description": "[STABLE] The number of available replicas per deployment."}
Question: What percentage of the coredns deployment's replicaset are currently ready in the cluster?
